          {
            "title": "Question: Appended at the end",
            "id": 82870,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Quale lista apparirà per prima nella lista unita?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"growth_rate_1 = [\" /><text value=\"0.5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.7\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"growth_rate_2 = [\" /><text value=\"0.8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(growth_rate_1 + growth_rate_2)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"[0.5, 0.7, 0.8, 0.8, 0.6, 0.6]\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>growth_rate_1</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>growth_rate_2</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Entrambe, perché la nuova lista avrà elementi mescolati casualmente</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>growth_rate_1</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Perché i tre valori di <code>growth_rate_1</code> appaiono prima di quelli di <code>growth_rate_2</code>?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"growth_rate_1 = [\" /><text value=\"0.5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.7\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"growth_rate_2 = [\" /><text value=\"0.8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(growth_rate_1 + growth_rate_2)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"[0.5, 0.7, 0.8, 0.8, 0.6, 0.6]\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Con <code>growth_rate_1 + growth_rate_2</code>, i valori della lista a sinistra vengono inseriti per primi.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Python inserisce la lista con il primo valore più piccolo prima dell'altra.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Le liste unite vengono mescolate e questo ordine è avvenuto casualmente.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Con <code>growth_rate_1 + growth_rate_2</code>, i valori della lista a sinistra vengono inseriti per primi.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Different types",
            "id": 82871,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Che cosa c'è che non va in questo codice?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"students_1 = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Anna&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"16\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Kim&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"16\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"students_2 = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Joe&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"17\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Lee&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"15\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(students_1 + students_2)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"['Anna', 16, 'Kim', 16, 'Joe', 17, 'Lee', 15]\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Non c'è nulla di sbagliato nel codice</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Non possiamo concatenare liste che contengono più tipi</item><item value=\"4\" correct=\"false\">Non possiamo avere numeri negli elenchi</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Non c'è nulla di sbagliato nel codice.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Dopo l'unione di queste liste, quale valore si trova all'indice <code>4</code> della nuova lista?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"students_1 = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Anna&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"16\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Kim&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"16\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"students_2 = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Joe&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"17\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Lee&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"15\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(students_1 + students_2)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"['Anna', 16, 'Kim', 16, 'Joe', 17, 'Lee', 15]\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>\"Joe\"</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>16</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Non c'è alcun risultato perché le liste contenenti stringhe e numeri non possono essere unite.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>\"Joe\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
